[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2164","id":4836053321,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT-9fds8AAAABIEBRSQ","html_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2164","diff_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2164.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2164.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2164","number":2164,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(R9): composed-verify's diagnostics leave stdout -- and the consume step degrades a foreign token to record-bare","user":{"login":"hpo-author[bot]","id":331381602,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOE8B7Yg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70032254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/hpo-author","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"composed-verify printed its \"was not composed this run\" diagnostic to\nstdout -- the same channel the Tests workflow's consume step word-splits\nas the script list. The diagnostic's first token, `composed-verify:`,\nbecame a fake script name in `$OUT`, and the step's bare `cp` died on it,\nturning the closures lane red on every pull-request head carrying a\ncomposed allow-list entry. This PR moves every composed-verify diagnostic\nto stderr (same words, right channel; stdout carries only the\nspace-separated script list, or empty) and hardens the consume loop so a\nforeign token degrades to record-bare -- printed and skipped, never a\nbare cp failure -- with `COMPOSED_CONSUMED` listing only what was\nactually consumed. Both sides of the contract are pinned by two new\nselftest arms, so neither side can regress silently.\n\n## Head\n\n`d72be540b96f996b1dc058e84b631bbb8b66d0fa` adds only the delivery row\n(`dev/programme/delivery/2164.md`, one line) onto the reviewed head\n`8ff131e854f035667e60bb55eb2cda0e508fc0b2` -- which merges main `59b7660`\ninto `07004ec78` (fix/composed-verify-stdout off origin/main d214c53a2),\nan automatic merge by the orchestrator, no resolution. The reviewed code\nis unchanged.\n\n## Mutation proof\n\nTwo mutations, each red on exactly its own arm, each restored after the\nrun (`python tests/closure.py selftest`):\n\n1. Diagnostic moved back to stdout (`file=sys.stderr` dropped):\n\n       FAIL composed-verify's stdout is exactly the script list; the not-composed diagnostic goes to stderr  [rc=0 out='composed-verify: tests/never_composed_here.py was not composed this run; it records bare\\ntests/boost_drift_replay.py\\n' err='']\n\n2. The workflow skip guard deleted:\n\n       FAIL the workflow loop skips a foreign token to record-bare and consumes only real stems  [rc=0 out=\"composed: consuming tests/boost_drift_replay.py's recording from this run's coverage job\\ncomposed: consuming composed-verify:'s recording from this run's coverage job\\n\" consumed='tests/boost_drift_replay.py composed-verify: ']\n\nThe second run's stdout is the pre-fix consume step staging the fake\ntoken -- exactly the state that killed the runner's cp.\n\n## Null control\n\nThe unmodified tree (origin/main d214c53a2) has no arms for these pins;\nits composed-verify behavior is mutation 1's output shape verbatim --\nthe diagnostic on stdout, `composed-verify:` as the first token of the\nword-split list -- and its consume loop is mutation 2's, which on the\nrunner is the cp failure quoted under Red checks. The consumed-recordings\nsemantics are unchanged when the list is clean: every token is a real\nstem, the guard's `[ -f ]` passes, and `COMPOSED_CONSUMED` accumulates\nthe identical string the old `printf '%s ' $OUT` produced;\n`tests/derive_closures.sh`'s match sees the same names, and a foreign\ntoken now yields an empty/shorter list, which records bare -- the\nstep's own fail-closed direction.\n\n## Figures\n\n    python tests/closure.py selftest   # ALL 95 closure shrink pins PASSED (2 new: the stdout-shape arm, the workflow-loop arm)\n    python tests/structure.py          # STRUCTURE RATCHET PASSED (all metrics flat or down)\n\n## Red checks\n\nThis defect turned PR heads' closures / closures-autofix / pr-contract\nchecks red -- a red on a file class those PRs did not touch, inherited\nfrom main's tool (#2132's job and tool together). Verified instance:\nTests job 115038269065 (run of `fix/prepr-closure-skip` at head\n03570d4be8), whose \"Verify and stage the composed recordings\" step ends\n\n    cp: cannot stat '/home/runner/work/_temp/composed/composed-verify:.json': No such file or directory\n\nCheaper detector, named: composed-verify's stdout-shape selftest arm\n(landed in this PR) -- standing cost approximately zero, it runs inside\nthe existing `python tests/closure.py selftest` that the scoped gate\nalready selects for `tests/closure.py`; no new job, no new runtime.\nProcess root cause, named: state (c) -- the process (the selftest)\nexisted and was followed, but pinned composed-verify's exit codes and\nrefusal lines, not the stdout channel the workflow word-splits; the\ncountermeasure is that arm, plus the workflow-side loop arm so a\nregression on either side of the contract is caught. These PR heads'\nreds clear when this fix is on main and they rebase or re-run.\n\n## Forward-carry\n\nnone\n\n## Friction\n\nnone\n\n","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:08:30Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T12:30:06Z","closed_at":"2026-10-13T12:30:04Z","merged_at":"2026-10-13T12:30:04Z","merge_commit_sha":"c613d00053950d37779262b072dbacda473946f1","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2164/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2164/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2164/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/statuses/d72be540b96f996b1dc058e84b631bbb8b66d0fa","head":{"label":"tvofi:fix/composed-verify-stdout","ref":"fix/composed-verify-stdout","sha":"d72be540b96f996b1dc058e84b631bbb8b66d0fa","user":{"login":"tvofi","id":70032254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMDMyMjU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70032254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi","html_url":"https://github.com/tvofi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1341087606,"node_id":"R_kgDOT-9fdg","name":"heatpump_o